      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND AND AIMS",
          "content": "Tulobuterol patch (Tulo) is often used for treatment of elder patient with asthma in Japan. However, there is no evidence either ICS plus Tulo or ICS/LABA combination is better for elder patient."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Elder patients with asthma (aged≥ 70, n=17) who had treated with budesonide (BUD) 400 μg/day plus Tulo 2 mg/day, were randomly assigned either to change control medication to budesonide/formoterol combination (BUD/FM) 320/9 μg/day or to keep BUD plus Tulo treatment for 12 weeks."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "At week 4 and week 12, the BUD/FM group showed significant increase in lung function (FEV1, %FEV1) and mini AQLQ score compared with the BUD plus Tulo group. The BUD/FM group also showed decrease in Tumor Necrosis Factor-alpha level in exhaled breath condensate at week 12. No adverse event was observed in both groups."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "In elder patients with asthma, treatment with BUD/FM does not have any clinical disadvantage and may provide better efficacy in lung function, QOL, and possibly anti-inflammation compared with BUD plus Tulo treatment."
        }
      ]},
